---
const digits = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, index) => {
  const digit = index + 1;
  const left = Math.log10(digit);
  const right = Math.log10(digit + 1);
  return {
    digit,
    left,
    width: right - left,
    probability: (right - left) * 100,
  };
});

const plotLeft = 72;
const plotWidth = 956;
---

<figure class="benford-strip reckoning-visual">
  <header>
    <p>One decade on a logarithmic ruler</p>
    <h3>Smaller first digits occupy wider intervals</h3>
  </header>

  <div class="strip-shell">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1100 370" role="img" aria-labelledby="benford-strip-title benford-strip-desc">
      <title id="benford-strip-title">Logarithmic intervals for decimal first digits</title>
      <desc id="benford-strip-desc">
        The interval from 1 to 2 occupies 30.1 percent of a base-ten logarithmic decade,
        while the interval from 9 to 10 occupies 4.6 percent. The intervening digit intervals
        decrease steadily in width.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <pattern id="benford-hatch" width="12" height="12" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(35)">
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="12" />
        </pattern>
      </defs>

      <g class="axis-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        {Array.from({ length: 11 }, (_, index) => (
          <line x1={plotLeft + (plotWidth * index) / 10} y1="82" x2={plotLeft + (plotWidth * index) / 10} y2="294" />
        ))}
      </g>

      <text class="axis-title" x={plotLeft} y="54">equal distance in log₁₀ space</text>
      <line class="axis" x1={plotLeft} y1="70" x2={plotLeft + plotWidth} y2="70" />
      <text class="axis-label" x={plotLeft} y="69" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text class="axis-label" x={plotLeft + plotWidth} y="69" text-anchor="middle">1</text>

      {digits.map(({ digit, left, width, probability }) => {
        const x = plotLeft + left * plotWidth;
        const pixelWidth = width * plotWidth;
        const center = x + pixelWidth / 2;
        return (
          <g class={`digit-segment digit-${digit}`}>
            <rect x={x} y="106" width={pixelWidth} height="148" rx="3" />
            <rect class="hatch" x={x} y="106" width={pixelWidth} height="148" rx="3" fill="url(#benford-hatch)" />
            <text class="digit" x={center} y="174" text-anchor="middle">{digit}</text>
            <text class="probability" x={center} y="210" text-anchor="middle">{probability.toFixed(1)}%</text>
            <line class="boundary" x1={x} y1="254" x2={x} y2="278" />
            <text class="boundary-label" x={x} y="301" text-anchor="middle">log {digit}</text>
          </g>
        );
      })}
      <line class="boundary" x1={plotLeft + plotWidth} y1="254" x2={plotLeft + plotWidth} y2="278" />
      <text class="boundary-label" x={plotLeft + plotWidth} y="301" text-anchor="middle">log 10</text>
      <path class="width-callout" d={`M${plotLeft} 326v14h${digits[0].width * plotWidth}v-14`} />
      <text class="callout-label" x={plotLeft + (digits[0].width * plotWidth) / 2} y="362" text-anchor="middle">log₁₀ 2 ≈ 0.301</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> the ordinary intervals from 1 to 2 and from 9 to 10 both
    have width 1. After a base-ten logarithm compresses the number line, the first interval is
    about 6.6 times as wide as the second. The labels and hatched fill make the comparison
    readable without relying on color.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .benford-strip {
    background: var(--surface-color);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    margin: 2.5rem 50%;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: min(1060px, calc(100vw - 3rem));
  }
  header > p {
    color: var(--link-color);
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.7rem);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .strip-shell {
    background: var(--bg-color);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 9px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  svg { display: block; height: auto; min-width: 760px; width: 100%; }
  .axis-grid line { stroke: var(--border-color); stroke-width: 1; }
  .axis { stroke: var(--text-secondary); stroke-width: 2; }
  .axis-title { fill: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .axis-label { fill: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 12px; }
  .digit-segment rect:first-child { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--link-color) 25%, var(--surface-color)); stroke: var(--link-color); stroke-width: 2; }
  .digit-segment:nth-of-type(even) rect:first-child { fill: color-mix(in srgb, #ff1493 16%, var(--surface-color)); stroke: #ff1493; }
  .hatch { opacity: 0.13; stroke: none; }
  #benford-hatch line { stroke: var(--text-primary); stroke-width: 2; }
  .digit { fill: var(--text-primary); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; }
  .probability { fill: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; }
  .boundary { stroke: var(--text-secondary); stroke-width: 1; }
  .boundary-label { fill: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 10px; }
  .width-callout { fill: none; stroke: #4f9300; stroke-width: 2; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .width-callout { stroke: #93ff14; }
  .callout-label { fill: #4f9300; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .callout-label { fill: #93ff14; }
  figcaption { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.55; margin-top: 0.85rem; }
  figcaption strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  @media (max-width: 500px) { .benford-strip { width: calc(100vw - 1.5rem); } }
</style>
